Subject: Same population, but with a few distinct items
Message-ID: <ghImjLp2E9s.ASw9Jf4vAwAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/ghImjLp2E9s/m/ASw9Jf4vAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Suppose we have the data from two exams applied to the same population:
Exam A: Has items 1 to 5 and 11 to 40.
Exam B: Has items 6 to 10 and 11 to 40.

Each individual answered exactly one of the exams (ie. individual 1 = answered exam A, individual 2 = answered exam B, individual 3 = answered exam B...)

How would I go about estimating the 3PL IRT parameters for these items using MIRT?

Best,
Pedro

